From d7a1eb6028f5d033849ec5c41ef9546256998ecb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:45:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] ogg: leave the header packets of an OggDS stream out of
 its data

An OggDS stream's header packets, its stream header and its comments, are
read again when a seek goes back to the stream's first pages, as a seek to
its start does. The headers were backed up on the way in and the stream is
no longer initializing, so the comment packet went to the decoder as the
first block of data. MediaCodec's MPEG-4 Part 2 output, which opens with
the aspect of the video object layer it finds in the first block, then
found none, and an OGM whose container states no aspect played square.

Drop a packet flagged as a header, after it has updated the clock as
before.
---
 modules/demux/ogg.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
index 1c8ed68..e025b1f 100644
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -1451,6 +1451,17 @@ static void Ogg_DecodePacket( demux_t *p_demux,
     /* Convert the granulepos into the next pcr */
     Ogg_UpdatePCR( p_demux, p_stream, p_oggpacket );
 
+    /* An OggDS stream's header packets, its stream header and its comments,
+     * are read again when a seek goes back to the stream's first pages, as a
+     * seek to its start does: they were taken as headers on the way in, and
+     * are no data. A decoder given one begins with it, before the first
+     * picture or sound: one that reads the stream's aspect from the first
+     * block it is given, as MediaCodec's MPEG-4 Part 2 output does from the
+     * video object layer, would find none there. */
+    if( p_stream->b_oggds && p_oggpacket->bytes > 0 &&
+        ( p_oggpacket->packet[0] & PACKET_TYPE_HEADER ) )
+        return;
+
     if( !b_selected )
     {
         /* This stream isn't currently selected so we don't need to decode it,
